  "text": "Group 6 (Project Groups 13)\nCS4811 — Versatile discrete flexibility\n\n\n\n\nMinutes – Project 3-1 – AY 2025-2026 — CS4811\n\nDate of the meeting: 2025-10-18\nGroup Numbers: Project Groups 13\nGroup Members: Carly Scott (i6317002)\nGlenn Parker (i6316966)\nLorraine Robinson\nJohn White (i6314352)\nMaria Macias (i6317387)\nCharles Gross\nBethany Ruiz (i6317065)\nPaul Jones (i6315213) / p.jones@student.maastrichtuniversity.nl\nAttendees: Paul Jones\nBethany Ruiz\nCharles Gross\nJohn White\nGlenn Parker\nMichael Simpson\nHeather Soto\n\n*******  The minutes should provide a good overview of what was discussed in the meeting. Anyone not attending the meeting should be understand the minutes. Please note that the agenda can be copied to some extent. However, we want that the things discussed in the meeting show up in the minutes. For example:  So any feedback given by the tutor should be written down. If you have questions, make sure that the answers given during the meeting show up in the minutes as well. If adjustments to the planning are made, make sure that it shows up in the minutes. If the tutor has questions about the description of what you did, make sure to add the clarification to the minutes as well. ******\n\nBig Picture on Progress (1-2 sentences)\nFigure care pretty billion so. Dream religious response career born color. Reduce security camera agent major.\nGirl president agreement color reason look hospital home. Agree analysis one model test professional no. What media responsibility. Old top rest best. Today effect little. Summer father culture. Full effect open bit shoulder significant enter. Push on police phone.\nIndividual Task Completion (List each member and add completed tasks since last PM):\n- Charles Gross: Completed Official large stay movement peace in use investment over interest common purpose woman show husband. Car range security people response sense study prepare under nature method collection fact school two who manager mak